    "fresh real PG database and Keycloak identity with signed ACTIVE authority; old state-map SQL wrapped before its DDL witnesses",
    "one-time CLOSED seal; unchanged SDK reads while CLOSED, rejects mutation, then commits under actual current identity authority",
    "close actually waits for in-flight write COMMIT; new SQL and TRUNCATE denied during drain/after durable closure",
    "real inverse business-row/gate lock order aborts later writer without deadlock, earlier writer commits and close finishes",
    "REPEATABLE READ snapshot taken while OPEN cannot write after close; real serialization failure",
    "actual APP cannot change private state, disable guards, set replica mode, advance sequence or create a large object",
    "cluster-global role capability drift is rejected in write trigger even though ALTER ROLE has no database DDL event",
    "CLOSED survives all application/control connection retirement; new unmodified SDK process connection still refused",
    "CAS rejects stale operation; same operation replay preserves revision; foreign system identity rejected",
    "actual wrong realm authority marker prevents OPEN; CLOSE still works without current IAM match",
    "rolled-back DDL still advances nontransactional epoch; unchanged catalog cannot silently reseal or reopen",
    "persisted DRAINING authority denies OPEN before API access",
    "actual authenticated whole-PGDATA cold recovery preserves catalog binding, committed state and CLOSED; fresh legacy SDK still denied",
    "unknown table causes coverage rejection; trusted SQL OPEN fault cannot bypass epoch guard; close remains available after drift"
